<article class="env-definition" id="00GW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00GW">Definition <span data-tag="00GW">10.37.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a domain. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An element $g$ of the fraction field of $R$ is called <em>almost integral over $R$</em> if there exists an element $r \in R$, $r\not= 0$ such that $rg^ n \in R$ for all $n \geq 0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The domain $R$ is called <em>completely normal</em> if every almost integral element of the fraction field of $R$ is contained in $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>